            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="FRA02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Sir</roleName>
                        <forename>Philip</forename>
                        <surname>Francis</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1740-10-22">
                        <placeName>Ireland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1818-12-23"/>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <occupation>political writer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin noted meeting Sir Philip Francis (1740–1818), politician and political writer (along with other whig supporters of <persName key="FOX01">Fox</persName>) in 1796, and the entries
    tie him to <persName key="LAU01">Lauderdale</persName>, <persName key="GRE01">Charles Grey</persName>, and <persName key="ROB04">Mary Robinson</persName>. 
    There is also an entry in 1821, but this is not coded as it is some time after Francis's death.</p>
                        <p>Godwin also recorded his death - on the 22nd of December 1818.</p>
                    </note>
